;; Configuration for the documentation site, read by the docs-engine
;; (https://github.com/jlt-commons/docs-engine).
;;
;; Build it locally with `bb site:build`/`bb site:serve` (added in
;; Phase 4 once the CI workflow that also uses it exists). CI builds
;; it on every push and pull request from .github/workflows/site.yml,
;; and publishes from main: the PUBLISH_SITE repository variable is
;; "true" and GitHub Pages is enabled.
{;; :base-path is what makes this a project site rather than an org
 ;; one. The site is served at
 ;; https://b12n-oss.github.io/lambda-mvp-bb/, so every URL the engine
 ;; emits needs that prefix. Leave it out and the pages still render,
 ;; but each one loads the ORGANIZATION site's stylesheet and every
 ;; asset 404s.
 :base-path   "/lambda-mvp-bb"

 :title       "lambda-mvp-bb"
 :description "A shareable AWS Lambda custom runtime in Babashka via blambda, with a bb bench tool for reproducing a cold-vs-warm boot-time comparison against your own AWS account."}
